  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-17T16:31:55.621Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "People really enjoy PvP combat, whether it's all a part of RP or a simple game, but as long as there may be a possible option to let players toggle their PvP status, like in some MMOs, e.g. World of Warcraft, players could really use something like this in pretty much any world. \n\nIn one of many possible scenarios, to make it work, VRChat needs to: \n1. Implement a system/module that would allow PvP in worlds with a specific status (for instance, it could be based on the \"pvp\" tag);\n2. Add a new UI element to allow players toggle their PvP status, which should be turned off by default;\n3. Provide users with objects used as weapons by following one of the possible options:\nA. Make a small set of items (guns, sharp objects, spells, etc.), out of which a player could spawn and use only one, with a reasonable cooldown rate;\nB. Let users make their own weapons, similarly to option A, containing colliders with special layers on objects that would deal damage to players on collision.\n4. Respawn players within 5 seconds after their \"death\".",
